================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Stop The Bar is a single-button precision/reflex game where a vertical bar 
slides back and forth across a horizontal track. The player must press the 
button at the exact right moment to "stop" the bar inside a highlighted 
target zone. Scoring rewards precision (hitting closer to the center of the 
zone earns more points), and the game features a lives system and streak 
tracking to encourage repeated attempts.

Unlike Flappy Bird (which is a continuous physics-based game), Stop The Bar 
is a TURN-BASED / ROUND-BASED game - each "round" is a single moving bar and 
a single button press, followed by a brief result display before the next 
round begins.

GAME GENRE     : Reflex / Precision Timing
CONTROL SCHEME : Single Button (Tap to Stop)
DIFFICULTY     : Progressive (zone shrinks & speed increases every 5-hit streak)
DISPLAY        : 128x64 OLED (SH1106 driver, SPI interface)
MICROCONTROLLER: Arduino Nano

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO PLAY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Power on the device - Start Screen appears showing "STOP THE BAR"
2. Press the button to begin the game
3. A vertical bar moves back and forth along a horizontal track
4. A highlighted "target zone" appears somewhere on the track
5. Press the button when the bar is INSIDE the target zone
6. Scoring is based on accuracy:
   - Hitting near the CENTER of the zone = more points
   - Hitting near the EDGE of the zone = fewer points (but still counts)
   - Missing the zone entirely = lose a life, streak resets to 0
7. Every 5 successful hits in a row (streak), the game gets harder:
   - Bar moves faster
   - Target zone becomes smaller
8. The game ends when all 3 lives are lost
9. Press the button again on the Game Over screen to restart

