5. FUNCTION-BY-FUNCTION BREAKDOWN
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.1 void setup()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Runs once at power-on. Initializes hardware and starts the first 
round.

WHAT IT DOES:
  1. Sets buttonPin as INPUT_PULLUP
  2. Initializes the OLED display
  3. Clears the display buffer
  4. Seeds the random number generator using analogRead(0)
  5. Calls setupRound() to configure the first round (bar position, 
     initial target zone)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.2 void setupRound()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Configures/resets variables needed at the START of each new round. 
Called both from setup() (first round) and from updateGame() (subsequent 
rounds after a result is shown).

WHAT IT DOES:
  1. Resets barX to 10 (left starting position)
  2. Resets barDir to 1 (moving right initially)
  3. Randomizes zoneStart to a new position between X=20 and 
     X=(128 - zoneWidth - 20) - this range ensures the zone always fits 
     on screen with margin
  4. Sets roundActive = true (bar begins moving, waiting for input)
  5. Sets showResult = false (clears any previous result feedback)

NOTE: This function does NOT reset score, lives, level, or streak - those 
persist across rounds within the same game session. Only resetGame() 
(Section 5.8) resets those.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.3 void loop()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Main game state machine, identical high-level structure to 
Flappy Bird's loop().

LOGIC FLOW:
  IF game has not started:
      -> Show start screen
      -> Check for button press to begin game
  ELSE IF game is running (not game over):
      -> Update game logic (bar movement, input, round management)
      -> Draw current frame
      -> Wait 20ms (controls animation/bar speed)
  ELSE (game over):
      -> Show game over screen with final score and best streak
      -> Check for button press to reset and play again

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.4 void updateGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Core game logic - handles bar movement, button edge detection, 
and round-to-round transitions. Called once per frame from loop().

SECTION-BY-SECTION BREAKDOWN:

  A) READ CURRENT BUTTON STATE
     bool currentButtonState = digitalRead(buttonPin);
     This is read once per frame and compared against lastButtonState 
     (from the PREVIOUS frame) later in this function.

  B) IF ROUND IS ACTIVE (bar is currently moving):
     - Bar position updates: barX += barDir * barSpeed
     - Boundary bounce logic:
         - If barX reaches the right edge (>= 124), clamp position and 
           reverse direction (barDir = -1)
         - If barX reaches the left edge (<= 0), clamp position and 
           reverse direction (barDir = 1)
     - EDGE DETECTION CHECK:
         if (currentButtonState == HIGH && lastButtonState == LOW)
         
         This specific pattern means: "the button was NOT pressed last 
         frame, but IS pressed THIS frame" - i.e., the exact moment of 
         a new button press. This prevents the game from registering 
         multiple hits if the player holds the button down, and ensures 
         checkResult() fires exactly ONCE per press.
     - If a new press is detected, checkResult() is called.

  C) IF SHOWING RESULT (roundActive is false, showResult is true):
     - Waits 800ms (checked via millis() - resultTime > 800)
     - After the wait:
         - If lives <= 0: game ends (gameOver = true)
         - Otherwise: setupRound() is called to start the next round

  D) UPDATE lastButtonState
     At the very end of the function, lastButtonState = currentButtonState 
     saves this frame's reading for comparison next frame. This line 
     MUST run every frame regardless of game state for edge detection 
     to work correctly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.5 void checkResult()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Called when the player presses the button during an active round. 
Determines hit/miss, calculates score, and updates game difficulty.

LOGIC BREAKDOWN:

  A) DETERMINE BAR CENTER POSITION
     int barCenter = barX + 2;
     (barX is the LEFT edge of the 4px-wide bar rectangle, so +2 gives 
     the approximate center point for accuracy calculations)

  B) CHECK IF BAR CENTER IS WITHIN THE TARGET ZONE
     if (barCenter >= zoneStart && barCenter <= zoneStart + zoneWidth)

     IF SUCCESS:
       - hitSuccess = true
       - streak increments; bestStreak updates if this is a new record
       - SCORING FORMULA:
           zoneCenter = zoneStart + zoneWidth / 2  (middle of the zone)
           distFromCenter = abs(barCenter - zoneCenter)  (how far off-center)
           points = max(1, 10 - distFromCenter)  (closer to center = more 
                    points, minimum 1 point guaranteed for any successful hit)
       - score += points
       - DIFFICULTY PROGRESSION: every 5 hits in the streak (streak % 5 == 0):
           - level increments
           - barSpeed increments (bar moves faster)
           - zoneWidth decreases by 2 (down to a minimum of 10px) - 
             makes future rounds harder to hit precisely

     IF MISS (bar center outside zone):
       - hitSuccess = false
       - streak resets to 0 (best streak is NOT affected, it's already saved)
       - lives decrements by 1

  C) TRANSITION TO RESULT DISPLAY STATE
     - roundActive = false (bar stops moving)
     - showResult = true (triggers "NICE HIT!"/"MISSED!" text display)
     - resultTime = millis() (starts the 800ms result display timer)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.6 void drawGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Renders the current frame to the OLED display.

DRAWING ORDER:
  1. Clear display buffer
  2. Draw the track: a hollow rectangle spanning the full screen width, 
     positioned at Y=30, height 8px (display.drawRect(0, 30, 128, 8, ...))
  3. Draw the target zone: a FILLED rectangle at the zone's position 
     (highlighting where the player needs to stop the bar), then an 
     additional outline drawn on top (mostly redundant but kept for 
     visual clarity/border emphasis)
  4. IF round is active: draw the moving bar as a filled rectangle 
     (4px wide, slightly taller than the track at Y=28 to Y=40, so it 
     visually "sticks out" above/below the track for visibility)
  5. IF showing result: display "NICE HIT!" or "MISSED!" text above 
     the track
  6. Draw HUD elements:
     - Score (top-left, "S:")
     - Level (top area, "L:")
     - Lives (top-right area, "Lives:")
     - Current streak (bottom-left, "Streak:")
     - Best streak (bottom-right, "Best:")
  7. Push frame to physical display

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.7 void drawStartScreen()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Displays the title/instruction screen before gameplay begins.

CONTENT SHOWN:
  - "STOP THE BAR" title at (20, 15)
  - "Press when bar is" instruction at (10, 30)
  - "in the zone!" continuation at (25, 40)
  - "Start" prompt at (45, 52)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.8 void drawGameOver()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Displays final results after all lives are lost.

CONTENT SHOWN:
  - "GAME OVER" at (30, 10)
  - "Score: [final score]" at (20, 25)
  - "Best Streak: [value]" at (20, 38)
  - "Press to Retry" at (15, 52)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.9 void resetGame()
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PURPOSE: Fully resets the game session for a new playthrough, called when 
the player presses the button on the Game Over screen.

RESET ACTIONS:
  - score back to 0
  - level back to 1
  - lives back to 3
  - streak back to 0
  - barSpeed back to 2
  - zoneWidth back to 25 (undoes difficulty shrinkage)
  - gameOver set to false
  - gameStarted set to false (returns to start screen)
  - setupRound() called to configure the first round of the new session

NOTE: bestStreak is intentionally NOT reset here, allowing it to persist 
as a "session high score" across multiple playthroughs until the Arduino 
is powered off/restarted. This is a deliberate design choice to encourage 
players to keep trying to beat their own best streak.

