9. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE: Multiple hits register from a single button press
FIX: This should NOT happen due to edge detection, but if it does, 
     verify that lastButtonState = currentButtonState; at the end of 
     updateGame() is executing every frame without being skipped by an 
     early return or conditional block.

ISSUE: Button press does nothing during gameplay
FIX: Check your button wiring polarity. If using a Normally Open button 
     with INPUT_PULLUP, a press should read LOW normally, but this code 
     checks for HIGH. Try changing "currentButtonState == HIGH" and 
     "lastButtonState == LOW" (and vice versa) to match your specific 
     wiring, OR simply swap the initial value of lastButtonState 
     accordingly.

ISSUE: Bar movement looks jumpy or inconsistent
FIX: Adjust the delay(20) value in loop() - this controls how often 
     the bar position updates. Smaller delay = smoother/faster movement.

ISSUE: Target zone sometimes appears partially off-screen
FIX: Check the random(20, 128 - zoneWidth - 20) range in setupRound(). 
     If zoneWidth becomes very small due to difficulty scaling, ensure 
     this formula still produces valid on-screen positions (shouldn't 
     be an issue with default values, but worth checking if you modify 
     zoneWidth's minimum floor).

ISSUE: Game feels too easy or too hard overall
FIX: The three main difficulty levers are: barSpeed (movement speed), 
     zoneWidth (target size), and the streak-based ramp-up interval 
     (currently every 5 hits). Adjust these together for balanced 
     difficulty tuning.

